## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `defaultValues` | `Partial<RetroOsAccountFormValues>` | empty name, user name, e-mail and password | Starting values, merged over an empty full name, user name, e-mail and password (their placeholders show) on Figma's Engineering, must change the password at next logon, a standard user and a lockout after 5 failed logons; `sampleRetroOsAccountValues` is the filled sample (Yusuf Hadi, `yhadi`, `yusuf@kopi.net`, an 8-character password). A department, account type or lockout that isn't in its list falls back to the first one. Cancel without `onCancel` puts these back. |
| `placeholders` | `Partial<RetroOsAccountFormPlaceholders>` | `"First and last name"`, `"jdoe"`, `"name@company.com"`, `"At least 8 characters"`, `"Optional"` | What the empty fields say, by field (`fullName`, `userName`, `email`, `password`, `description`). |
| `onSubmit` | `(values, helpers) => void \| Promise<void>` | – | Called by OK and Apply once the fields are valid (names and e-mail trimmed). `helpers` is `{ action: "ok" \| "apply", progress(value, label?) }`: report a percentage and what's happening and the status bar shows it (the steps stop). A rejection shows "Account not created. Try again." and keeps the dialog. OK with nothing changed since the last Apply doesn't call it again. |
| `onCancel` | `() => void` | puts the defaults back | Cancel and the Escape key. |
| `onClose` | `() => void` | `onCancel` | The title bar's ×, and OK on the message box (without it, that OK starts a new account). |
| `title` | `string` | `"New User Account"` | The title bar (Silkscreen) and the message box; also the form's accessible name. |
| `departments` / `accountTypes` / `lockoutOptions` | `RetroOsAccountOption[]` | the samples | `{ value, label }` lists for Department, Account type (radio buttons) and Lock after. |
| `takenUserNames` | `string[]` | `admin`, `administrator`, `guest`, `root`, `system` | User names that are refused ("is already taken"). |
| `steps` | `RetroOsAccountStep[]` | Creating account... 24%, Creating home folder... 64%, Setting permissions... 92% | `{ label, value }` the status bar walks through while `onSubmit` runs, until it reports its own progress. |
| `stepDuration` | `number` | `700` | Milliseconds per step. |
| `homeFolder` | `(userName: string) => string` | `` C:\Users\<user> `` | Shown on the General tab and in the message box. |
| `defaultPictureName` | `string` | `"robot.bmp"` | The name shown while the default picture (the pixel robot) is in use. |
| `maxPictureSize` | `number` | 2 MB | Larger pictures are refused. |
| `tab` / `defaultTab` / `onTabChange` | `RetroOsAccountTab` | `"profile"` | The open tab (`"general"`, `"profile"` or `"security"`), controlled or not. |

`RetroOsAccountFormValues` is `{ picture, fullName, userName, email, department, password, mustChangePassword, disabled, description, accountType, passwordNeverExpires, lockout }`; `picture` is the picked `File` (null for the default) and `passwordNeverExpires` is always false while `mustChangePassword` is on. Other props go to the `<form>` (`className`, `style` and `onKeyDown` are merged, `ref` reaches the form). The file also exports the sample data (`sampleRetroOsAccountValues`, `sampleRetroOsAccountDepartments`, `sampleRetroOsAccountTypes`, `sampleRetroOsAccountLockout`, `sampleRetroOsAccountSteps`) and the types `RetroOsAccountFormProps`, `RetroOsAccountFormValues`, `RetroOsAccountFormPlaceholders`, `RetroOsAccountOption`, `RetroOsAccountStep`, `RetroOsAccountSubmitHelpers` and `RetroOsAccountTab`.

## Notes

- Validation: a full name; a user name of 3–20 of a–z, 0–9, ".", "_" and "-" starting with a letter and not in `takenUserNames`; a valid e-mail; a password of at least 8 characters; a picture that is an image under `maxPictureSize`. Errors turn the label red, add a message linked with `aria-describedby` and set `aria-invalid`; every checked field is on the Profile tab, so an invalid submit opens it, focuses the first field and shakes the window. A message goes away as the field is fixed.
- Keyboard: Enter in a field presses OK (the default button, drawn with the dark outline in the dark theme), Escape cancels, the tabs and the account type move with the arrow keys, the lists open with Enter, Space or the arrows, Space toggles a check box. Focus shows the dotted rectangle classic dialogs draw (Figma draws none). The status bar is a `progressbar` with its text as `aria-valuetext`, and announces changes politely; the message box is an `alertdialog` that takes focus.
- While `onSubmit` runs the cursor is an hourglass (`cursor: wait`), the fields are read-only and the buttons ignore presses, but nothing greys out, as on the old systems.
- Light by default and dark under your app's `.dark` class (the form sets its own color-scheme; its palette holds light-dark() pairs from the Figma light 2713:27413 and dark 1891:83066 frames). The light frame draws the title bar, tabs, panel, picture, OK and Cancel without a fill or bevel, so those bevels are dark only, and its 1px lines (round the window, the tab strip and the picture's name) only exist in light.
- Re-skin it through the CSS variables on the form: `--os-window`, `--os-tab` (the tabs at rest), `--os-face` (the panel, the open tab, OK and Cancel), `--os-button` (the other buttons), `--os-title-icon`, `--os-well`, `--os-picture`, `--os-cell` (the empty progress segments), `--os-strip` and `--os-line` (light's tab strip and caption box, and its 1px lines), `--os-text`, `--os-text-2`, `--os-disabled`, `--os-accent`, `--os-check` (check marks and the picked option), `--os-title-from`, `--os-title-to`, `--os-title-text`, `--os-selection` and `--os-on-selection` (selected text, the highlighted list item), `--os-groove` and `--os-groove-shadow`, `--os-frame` (the default button's outline), the bevel colours `--os-highlight`, `--os-shade`, `--os-well-shade` and `--os-well-light`, `--os-shadow` (the window's shadow), `--os-danger` and `--os-success`. The lists portal to `<body>` and copy them, and the form's color-scheme, when they open.
- The dialog is as wide as its container up to 480px (the Figma width); the title bar's □ widens it to the container. Under 400px the label column narrows to 84px and the panel's padding to 12px; long option labels wrap beside their box.
- Installs Silkscreen (`forms-pro-font-silkscreen`, the title) and JetBrains Mono (`forms-pro-font-jetbrains-mono`, the rest, regular and medium). The ✓, □ and ▾ are inline SVGs traced from Figma, because the web fonts' subsets don't include them.
- With `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing animates; React always renders the final state, so the server render is complete too.
- Figma: the form is "Modal" (1891:83067) inside "Stage / 12 Retro OS" (1891:83066), section "Premium ($14)" on page "Page 7". Figma draws the dialog mid-Apply ("Creating home folder... 64%") with the caret in User name; the dialog opens with its fields empty, so the playground's shot shows it at rest ("Ready.") with the caret in User name. The placeholders, the General and Security tabs, the errors, the lists, the finished and failed states, the message box, the disabled Apply, the rolled-up and widened window and the focus rectangles are designed here in the dialog's own language. Errors are red (`#ff6b6b`, light `#dc2626`) and "Account created" green (`#6fdc8c`, light `#1b9346`); Figma has neither. The light frame leaves the title white on its white title bar, so light draws the title in the text colour instead.

A glass sheet for sending a token: pick the token, the network and a saved recipient from their menus (or press the pencil and type a 0x address or an ENS name), enter the amount (Max fills the balance, and a USD estimate follows as you type), pick Slow, Standard or Fast, and read what the recipient gets, the gas fee and the token contract, every number computed from the choices: the fee is the network's standard fee times the speed's multiplier, the arrival time comes from the speed, and sending the network's own coin keeps the fee back from the balance. "Review transfer" validates (an amount above zero and within the balance, a valid recipient; errors under the fields, the first problem focused, the sheet shakes), shows "Sending…", then a green "Sent … to …" note and a check in place of the lock, with "New transfer" to start again. Everything moves with anime.js: the sheet rises in under its light beams and halftone, the rings and the lock node pop, the rings breathe while the sheet is on screen, the gauge needle swings to the picked speed, the gas fee counts to its new value, and sending pulses the node and draws the check.

