  )
}
```

## API

`useControllableState<T>({ value?: T; defaultValue: T; onChange?: (value: T) => void }) => readonly [T, (next: T) => void]`

## Notes

- Controlled when `value` is not `undefined`; the setter then only calls `onChange`. Uncontrolled, it also updates its own state.
- The setter takes a value, not an updater function.

